  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What queue mode changes",
      "items": [
        "The main n8n process takes the webhook and enqueues the run in Redis",
        "A worker, not the main process, executes lead-intake and process-lead",
        "n8n-worker extends the n8n service, so key, database and mounts match"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What stays the same",
      "items": [
        "WordPress, the outbox and the cron sidecar are unchanged",
        "Idempotency still lives in Postgres processed_events; the main process keeps workflows and credentials there too",
        "Redis has no published port and no password: add one before production"
      ]
    }
  ]
